cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you replicate, build on, or benchmark against this repository
  (the capacity meter, the deterministic integer training battery,
  the gate protocols, or any booked result), cite it as below AND
  pin the exact commit: every citation must name the git commit
  sha (and tag, if any) it relies on. The lab is a living ledger:
  results are never edited in place but are corrected by dated
  AMENDMENT entries, so an unpinned citation is unverifiable. The
  verdict-by-verdict ledger (docs/RESULTS.md) is the citable record;
  name the specific verdict entry plus the commit sha that contains
  it.
title: "llmopt: an oracle-verified mathematics and physics ML lab"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Artin
    family-names: Azizi
    alias: 39hops
repository-code: "https://github.com/39hops/llmopt"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - reproducible-research
  - symbolic-mathematics
  - deterministic-computing
  - fixed-point-arithmetic
  - mixture-of-experts
  - quantization
  - verified-search
